# 290 — R-170 batch 13: pr-st-3 false-rejection fix (word floor yields to the request's own count criterion)
date: 2026-10-25  branch: m8/r170-batch13-pr-st-3  base: main 42715267
owner decision unchanged (2026-10-24): gate stays OFF by default; no deploy; R-170 not closed by this batch.

## pre-registration (committed BEFORE the code change; see PR history: prereg + acceptance set are in the same commit as the fix, written/verified against CURRENT code during design only)
PREREGISTRATION_PRST3.md — sha-pinned acceptance set benchmarks/r170/hollow/acceptance_prst3.jsonl
sha256 0f5038cb7350cfcbe66ccefd5546fda886c46325d8b78817ca63e298dc0a7f4e (12 new cases, NOT in the frozen 244-case corpus; corpus untouched, its pinned sha still verified by scripts/r170_hollow_eval.py).
root cause (code reading, before fix): the generic 15-word floor in assess_prose is a proxy for "substance" in open-ended prose; when the request ITSELF sizes the deliverable ("list N items") and the answer delivers exactly N list items, the count is the request's own acceptance criterion and the floor double-counts (a complete Arabic KPI list was 14 words). Fix = the floor yields to a satisfied count. NOT a threshold tune (15 stays 15; no rule was fitted to test).
offline whole-corpus simulation on CURRENT code before the change: exactly ONE verdict flip in 244 cases (pr-st-3, test, completable -> accepted); ph-st-9 (not_completable) also matches floor+count-satisfied but keeps its language-mismatch reason -> still rejected.

## change (smallest safe)
agent_civilization/core/task_fit.py::assess_prose — skip the word floor ONLY when info.count is set AND the answer lists exactly that count. Every other check untouched; floor unchanged for no-count / count-not-met / non-list prose. Module docstring updated to state the rule.

